WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.103
WIL WILLIS: Blade
smiths, congratulations.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.606
You made it through a really
brutal round of testing.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:10.176
And now here you are,
that much closer to being

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.611
"Forged in Fire" champions.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.580
Well, now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.714
to recreate this iconic weapon.

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:16.782
Ready to see what it is?

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:17.516
 Oh, yeah.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.418
 Yeah.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.653
[ninja sounds]

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.421
 Yah!

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.658
 The nine ring broadsword.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.629
Good luck, blade smiths.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.829
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:31.530
 Thank you.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.298
 Good luck.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.336
BURTON: It's day one
here at the home forge.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.605
I don't really have much
experience making something

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:43.143
this big or this wide.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.845
The plan for today is I've got
to get to the end of the sword

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.580
drawn out quite a ways.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.615
I'm going to use 1080 steel.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.216
Nice big heavy bar of it.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.320
1080 is nice, hard steel
that's forgiving for heat

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.523
treatment in an open forge.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:57.923
Let her start warming up.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.860
I'm doing most of the
work on the press.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.661
My plan is, just
to kind of get it

00:01:02.761 --> 00:01:06.165
worked out a little bit here.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:09.935
Just trying to break that
down and spread it out.

00:01:10.035 --> 00:01:11.504
Heat her back up.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.239
It has to be a minimum
of two and a half

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.174
to four inches from the tip.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.508
So I'm going to go for
three, that way I've

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:18.945
got a little bit of
movement to do any tweaks

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:22.848
I need to after heat-treat.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.018
I'm halfway there, maybe.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.386
Yeah, tip's coming
right in there now.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.222
It's starting to take
shape of a sword.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.457
That's it for day one.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.663
 We are at my home forge.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.164
I start forging the blade today.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:41.034
And I'm looking to have it
fully forged hopefully midday

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.302
tomorrow to where I can
start doing some grinding.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.238
My biggest concern with
this blade is heat-treat.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:48.173
I'd really, really hate
to have to start over

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.243
again at the end of day two.

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:51.411
I've got a lot of
meat in this thing

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.245
that needs to be thinned out.

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:55.682
Fortunately, I have a power
hammer that's going to help

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.283
a lot with making that happen.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.451
Oh, you've got to be
[bleep] kidding me.

00:01:59.551 --> 00:02:01.253
All of a sudden, my
power hammer decides it

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:02.221
doesn't want to play anymore.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.522
It stops working.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.191
That sucks.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.692
So in-between heats
now, I'm trying

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.060
to rewire my power hammer.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.262
All right, well,
that ain't working.

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.931
Finally get the
switch back together.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:12.898
Ta-da.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:14.299
It's alive.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.201
So I'm working on the
blade and drawing it out.

00:02:16.301 --> 00:02:18.271
And I notice there's
a crack in the blade.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:22.074
[sigh] And there's
no saving this.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.610
Yeah, it's junk.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.811
So my back-up steel is 01.

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:27.046
It is a tool steel.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.481
But it's not a good
steel for swords.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.149
Hopefully I can temper it
right and it'll still hold

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:31.284
together through the testing.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:36.655 line:0%
BURTON: It's day
two for me today.

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.158 line:0%
I'm going to go ahead and
take some of the 3/16 rod.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.694
And we'll scroll and jig
and try to set up some,

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.196
like, inch and a half rings.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.899
I'm going to hot cut
them off one at a time.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.633
Once they get
attached on the sword,

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.136
then I'll just give
them a little TIG weld

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:51.770
to hold them together on there.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:54.240
We're getting ready try to
drill the holes for the rings.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:57.043
It could have possibly got
too hard in the forging.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:03:00.212
Find out here in a second.

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:02.314
Looks like it's
drilling like butter.

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:05.451
First two holes drill just fine.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.752
[grinding noise]

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.054
That's harder.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:11.958
[bleep] Oh, I was hoping
they would drill easy.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:12.958
[grinding noise]

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:14.226
That's what I was afraid of.

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:16.328
It can't be a nine
ring sword without nine

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:18.163
holes for the rings to go in.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.700
Feeling the clock now.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.135
It's not soft.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.070
I'm going to heat the spine
of it up with the torch

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.205
and try to just draw it
back and hopefully it'll

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.941
be soft enough that I
can get those last seven

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:30.276
holes punched through it.

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.779
If this doesn't
work, I'm screwed.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.815 line:7%
I'd hate to start forging again.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.583 line:0%
MIKE: There's still a heck
of a lot of work to do.

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:40.453
So it's critical that I really
hit the heat-treat tonight.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.921
If it breaks, if
it cracks, if it

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:45.024
does anything other than
quenches hard and straight,

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.460
I'm done.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.762
I have no backups anymore.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.663
We've got a hard blade.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.431
It's straight.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:57.469
So as I started
profiling the blade more,

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:01.975
all of a sudden I notice
something's gone wrong again.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.609
I've got a [bleep]
crack in the blade.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.344
I have no more
steel to work with.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.613
All right, so how do I fix that?

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:10.016
I decide to just put scallops
in between all of the eyelets

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.851
for the rings, and hopefully
grind far enough down where

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:15.087
I'm beyond where the crack is.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.121
No more crack.

00:04:16.221 --> 00:04:17.457
Doesn't look like the picture.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.659
But i kind of like it,
to tell you the truth.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.197
 I got some sweet tea.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.699
Day four, finally punched
through the last hole.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.501
So now we've got a
nine hole broadsword.

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:32.037
Got the sword
quenched yesterday.

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:33.639
But I'm still under the gun.

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:37.109
Time to get all these
rings welded on here.

00:04:37.175 --> 00:04:39.945
Does rattle-- they're on there.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:43.983
I'm going to use a camo color
para cord to do the wrap.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.119
And it gives enough grip
and thickness to the handle.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.655
[laughs] Thing's beastly.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.925
I'm finished.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:53.959
It's sharp.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:54.994
It's an instrument of death.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.028
It's a wild thing.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.464 line:7%
Thing looks wicked.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.566 line:0%
MIKE: First thing I'm
getting after is the rings.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.101
I'm going with eighth-inch
[inaudible] steel.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.137
I created a jig a while back
for bending this kind of stuff.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.672
I'm going to put
it in the jig, bend

00:05:06.738 --> 00:05:10.876
them around until they're pretty
symmetrical and pretty even.

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:12.412
Yeah, not too bad.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:15.781
So all I have left to do is get
these rings welded in place.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.983
Boy, that looks like
[bleep] it just doesn't want

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.552
to weld together very well.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.454
I mean, it starts to melt.
It starts to do other things.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.321
Damn it.

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:24.023
But finally, blade's finished.

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:25.958
Nine ring broadsword, brother.

00:05:26.024 --> 00:05:27.193
I love this thing.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:28.294
I'd like to keep it,
put it on my wall.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.663
But I'd rather have 10 grand.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:35.535
 Blade smiths, you
have our gratitude.

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:43.075
Gentlemen, your swords
look magnificent.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.544
But are they deadly?

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:47.546
To find that out, we
will take your swords

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:51.350
and deliver some clean
blows on this pig carcass.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:54.052
It's all about the kill
in this particular test.

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:56.288
Burton, you are first.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:57.156
Are you ready, sir?

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.324
 Yes, sir.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:00.360
 Let's do this.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.828
 Pretty much what could go
wrong is the blade breaks

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.998
or it's not sharp enough to
cut what it's supposed to cut.

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:09.301
Let's see how it holds up.

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:13.373
[dramatic music]

00:06:22.147 --> 00:06:24.049
 Damn.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.919
[dramatic music]

00:06:39.898 --> 00:06:43.235
[gasps]

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:44.771
 Well, there it went.

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:50.676
 Goodness, look at that.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:55.013
 All right, Burton.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:07:00.553
First up, what I love about
this blade was the balance,

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:04.590
the way I was able to move
with the blade everywhere.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.725
Now let's talk
about the breakage.

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:09.595
OK, so the break
happened right there,

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.697
where the ring was attached.

00:07:11.763 --> 00:07:14.033
You can see it's
really not a bad core

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:15.067
structure you have there.

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:16.335
It could be finer.

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:17.937
But rings, when you're
digging into that

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:19.605
could cost stress risers--

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:22.041
and it broke right
there with the ring was.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.980
Well, gentlemen, the
fight is not over.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:32.284
Because Mike, your blade still
has to survive nine strikes

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.186
on its kill test target.

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:35.588
Good luck, gentlemen.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:36.856
Doug?

00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:39.158
MIKE: Burton's blade broke
right at one of the holes.

00:07:39.224 --> 00:07:40.459
I have them same holes in there.

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:43.262
Plus on my spine, I've
already had two cracks.

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:44.730
I'm terrified it's
going to break.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.567
Oh, the heart's starting
to flutter a little bit.

00:07:57.376 --> 00:08:02.882 line:7%
[dramatic music]

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:32.645
 Good job, bro.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:43.121
 Burton, unfortunately your
blade broke and it can no

00:08:43.221 --> 00:08:44.856
longer continue with testing.

00:08:44.956 --> 00:08:49.461
And for that reason, I have
to dismiss you from the forge.

00:08:49.528 --> 00:08:50.763
Good job, brother.
- I appreciate it, man.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:51.463
 That sucks.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:52.431
 [inaudible]

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:53.799
 Gorgeous weapon, though.

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:56.602
 Seeing my blade break,
it's a disappointment.

00:08:56.668 --> 00:08:59.071
You know, you make it to
round three, you want to win.

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:02.073
You know, them nine holes
burnt through four drill bits

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.309
doing them.

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:04.543
So somewhere through
there, I probably

00:09:04.643 --> 00:09:06.044
was giving a little
too much pressure

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:09.281
and caused the stress riser
to run down that blade.

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:12.618
That was enough to cause a
critical failure in that blade.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.619
I'm still proud of myself
with what I've done.

00:09:14.719 --> 00:09:17.489
You know, it was way
out of my wheelhouse.

00:09:17.556 --> 00:09:19.191
What's next for
me is not swords,

00:09:19.257 --> 00:09:22.628
especially nine ring swords,
[laughs] that's for damn sure.

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:26.865
WIL WILLIS: Mike,
congratulations.

00:09:26.965 --> 00:09:28.734
The strength and
integrity of your blade

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:31.303
has made you a "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.340
And that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:34.406 --> 00:09:35.374
Good job, brother.

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:37.275
[clapping]

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:38.844
 I won 'Forged in Fire."

00:09:38.945 --> 00:09:40.078
Holy crap, man.

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:41.480
 Come on forward and
shake our hands, my friend.

00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:42.648
 Thank you.
Thank you.

00:09:42.715 --> 00:09:44.182
- Good job, brother.
- Thank you.

00:09:44.249 --> 00:09:45.951
With some of the things that
went wrong in my home forge,

00:09:46.017 --> 00:09:47.920
I was really sure that that
blade was going to break on me.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:51.457
But it didn't.
(SINGING) Da da da.

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:53.659
This is a happy dance.

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:55.527
Doing a little dance.

00:09:55.628 --> 00:09:59.699
[music playing]

